{"schema":1,"function":"laplace_ppf","description":"Laplace distribution quantile function mu + b log(2p) (p <= 1/2), mu - b log(2 - 2p) (p > 1/2)","inputs":["mu","b","p"],"outputs":["y"],"points":174,"tolerance":{"rel":1e-13,"reason":"p is an exact double, and so are 2p and 2 - 2p (Sterbenz), so a careful method forms L = log(2p) or log(2 - 2p) within an ulp; then mu + b L costs (|mu| + |b L|) / |mu + b L| ulps, at most about 14 on this grid (mu = 100, b = 8, p = 1e-5; tested), 1.6e-15. 1e-13 as for the other quantiles"},"grid":"(mu, b) in {(0, 1), (0, 2^-500), (0, 2^500), (-10, 1/4), (100, 8), (-2^1023, 2^1023)} x the gamma_ppf probabilities (p = 0, 5e-324, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-50, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4, 1/2 - 1e-10, 1/2, 1/2 + 1e-10, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999, 1 - 1e-5, 1 - 1e-10, 1 - 1e-15 and 1) and the doubles next to 1/2 (1/2 - 2^-54, 1/2 + 2^-53); p = 0 and 1 are tagged pole (-inf and +inf), quantiles beyond the largest double are tagged overflow","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.laplace.ppf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
